   <media:description>This video is about Team ORIon's participation in the 2022 RoboCup held in Bangkok, Thailand. RoboCup is an international robotics competition that promotes research in robotics and AI. Team ORIon, supported by the ORI, the Department of Engineering Science, and private donors, sent nine members to compete in the &quot;@Home&quot; domestic standard platform league. In this league, the robots have to assist humans in household environments by performing tasks such as greeting guests, storing groceries, and taking out the garbage. The competition required the integration of the robot's navigation, task-level planning, manipulation, voice recognition, vision, and semantic mapping capabilities. Check out the link to learn more about Team ORIon and their achievements. 

